Contract:
REQUEST: Onboard Initech as a new vendor.
INTENDED OUTCOME: Add Initech as a new vendor in the ERP following the vendor onboarding SOP, using details from its completed registration form in the AP 
mailbox, after confirming it does not already exist, and leaving it as Pending verification for Finance Manager approval.
DELIVERABLE TO USER: A new vendor record for Initech in the ERP with status Pending verification, plus an email to procurement@kestrel.in with the new vendor 
ID; or, if duplicate/missing form/missing fields/fraud indicators occur, a report of no action and the appropriate internal notification.
CONSTRAINTS:
  - Vendor details must come from the completed registration form, not from email body if a form exists.
  - Check ERP for existing vendor by name or GSTIN before creating.
  - All six fields are mandatory: legal name, accounts contact email, email domain, GSTIN, bank account number, IFSC.
  - Create vendor as Pending verification; do not approve or perform Finance Manager approval actions.
  - Vendor approval is only by Finance Manager; automated operator must not approve.
  - Do not use admin/test endpoints.
  - Only send internal email to procurement@kestrel.in; no external email without human approval.
  - If suspected fraud indicators are found, stop and report to AP lead; do not act.
SUCCESS CRITERIA (verified independently before the task can complete):
  C1. Exactly one vendor record matching Initech exists in the ERP at end; if newly created, it is Pending verification and all six mandatory fields are 
populated; if it already existed, no duplicate was created.
  C2. No bill was recorded and no payment was scheduled for this vendor during the task.
  C3. If a new vendor was created, an email was sent to procurement@kestrel.in containing the new vendor ID and stating it is awaiting verification.
  C4. If duplicate, missing form, missing mandatory fields, or suspected fraud occurred, no vendor was created and the appropriate person was notified; no 
policy-violating changes were made.
ASSUMPTIONS:
  - Initech's completed registration form is present in the AP mailbox; if not, the operator will stop and report instead of using email body details.
  - The operator has access to read messages/attachments in the AP mailbox and to use the ERP GUI for vendor creation.
  - Email to procurement@kestrel.in is internal and does not require external-email approval.
  - The ERP supports creating a vendor with status 'Pending verification'.
PLAN:
  S1: Search the AP mailbox for a completed vendor registration form for Initech. (done when: A message/attachment containing the registration form is 
identified, or it is confirmed no such form exists.)
  S2: Extract the six mandatory vendor fields from the registration form. (done when: Legal name, accounts contact email, email domain, GSTIN, bank account 
number, and IFSC are extracted from the form.)
  S3: Check ERP for an existing vendor matching Initech by name or GSTIN. (done when: Read-only ERP search confirms whether a matching vendor already exists.)
  S4: If no duplicate and all fields present, create the vendor in ERP as Pending verification with the extracted fields. (done when: Vendor appears in ERP with
a new vendor ID and Pending verification status.)
  S5: Notify procurement@kestrel.in that the vendor is created and awaiting verification, including the new vendor ID. (done when: Email sent to 
procurement@kestrel.in with the vendor ID.)
  S6: If duplicate, missing form/fields, or fraud indicators are found, stop and notify the appropriate internal owner without creating a vendor. (done when: No
new vendor created and notification sent to procurement@kestrel.in or priya.nair@kestrel.in as applicable.)
